From: rcllf local patch
Subject: [PATCH] federate: discard an RTI message past the stop tag, keep the RTI connection

handle_tagged_message() discards a message that arrives when the federate is
already at its stop tag, then closes `net` and returns -1. For a peer-to-peer
connection (decentralized) that ends one listener thread. Under centralized
coordination every message comes through the RTI connection (fed_id -1): the
branch closed the RTI connection itself, and listen_to_rti_net() treats the -1
as a failed read and calls lf_print_error_and_exit(), that is exit() on the RTI
listener thread. A message tagged past the stop tag is legal here: a federate
sends at its last tag before the stop through an `after` delay, the RTI may
grant the receiver its stop tag first (the delay allows it), and the message
then arrives after the stop.

The exit() runs the program's atexit handlers on the listener thread while the
main thread still runs its own shutdown, and a worker thread that next sends a
tag to the closed connection calls exit() as well (seen in a trace from a two-board run).
In an rcllf federate that handler list holds the ROS 2 teardown
(ros2_lf_runtime_shutdown), so DDS entities are torn down off the main thread
and concurrently: "Failed to delete datareader", then
std::system_error "Invalid argument" (abort, exit -6) or SIGSEGV
(exit -11). Without ROS the federate still exits 1 after a
correct stop.

The fix discards such a message from the RTI (fed_id -1) before that branch,
frees its token, logs a warning and returns 0, so the RTI connection stays
open for the stop and resign protocol. The peer-to-peer branch is unchanged.

Upstream reactor-c main still closes the connection (checked 2026-10-30,
commit 6003cd312).
---
--- a/core/federated/federate.c
+++ b/core/federated/federate.c
@@ -633,6 +633,27 @@
        // For decentralized coordination, this is needed to unblock the STAA.
     update_last_known_status_on_input_port(env, actual_tag, port_id, true);
 
+    // rcllf: under centralized coordination every message
+    // comes through the RTI connection (fed_id -1). A message tagged past the
+    // stop tag of a federate that has already reached it is discarded HERE and
+    // the RTI connection stays open: the branch below closes `net`, which is the
+    // RTI connection, and its -1 makes listen_to_rti_net() call
+    // lf_print_error_and_exit(), i.e. exit() on the RTI listener thread while the
+    // main thread still runs the program's shutdown (abort or SIGSEGV).
+    if (fed_id == -1 && lf_tag_compare(env->current_tag, env->stop_tag) >= 0 && env->execution_started) {
+      lf_print_warning("Discarding a message from the RTI tagged past the stop tag.\n"
+                       "    Current tag is " PRINTF_TAG " and intended tag is " PRINTF_TAG ".",
+                       env->current_tag.time - start_time, env->current_tag.microstep,
+                       intended_tag.time - start_time, intended_tag.microstep);
+      // Freshly allocated and never scheduled (ref_count 0): free it directly.
+      _lf_free_token(message_token);
+#ifdef FEDERATED_DECENTRALIZED
+      _lf_decrement_tag_barrier_locked(env);
+#endif
+      LF_MUTEX_UNLOCK(&env->mutex);
+      return 0;
+    }
+
     // If the current time >= stop time, discard the message.
     // But only if the stop time is not equal to the start time!
     if (lf_tag_compare(env->current_tag, env->stop_tag) >= 0 && env->execution_started) {
